{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_54","type":"agent_message","text":"Disassembly shows the cause: release optimization inlined `create_state` into Rust `confusion` and eliminated the heap-allocated `ProcessState`, so Rust allocates only the 128-byte buffer while C first allocates the 24-byte state. I’m preventing that cross-entry-point optimization so allocation order and failure propagation remain part of the translated ABI behavior."}}
